1. The cuboid is \(3\times2\times2=12\) cubes, so the three pieces contain \(4\) cubes each.
2. Tracing the grey and dark pieces leaves the white cubes arranged on the back layer as:

\[
\begin{array}{ccc}
\text{grey}&\text{white}&\text{dark}\\
\text{white}&\text{white}&\text{white}
\end{array}
\]

3. Thus, the white piece consists of three cubes in a row with a fourth cube attached above the middle cube—a T-shaped piece.
4. Rotating this piece to match the orientation of the red reference marks gives the arrangement in choice B.

\[
\boxed{\text{B}}
\]
